<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">stamina</ansi>

Stamina represents your physical endurance and is a critical resource in combat and
exploration. Managing stamina effectively is the key to survival in extended fights.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ What is Stamina? ━━━</ansi>

Stamina is your physical energy pool, used for:
  - Defensive actions (dodge, parry, block)
  - Special combat moves (bash, trip, kick)
  - Standing up when knocked prone
  - Movement and other physical activities

<ansi fg="stat">Maximum Stamina:</ansi> Based on your Vitality stat
<ansi fg="stat">Regeneration:</ansi> Regenerates slowly during combat, faster while resting

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Stamina Costs ━━━</ansi>

Every defensive action and special move costs stamina:

  <ansi fg="stat">Defensive Actions (per attempt):</ansi>
  - Dodge: 2 stamina (cheapest defense)
  - Parry: 4 stamina (requires weapon)
  - Block: 5 stamina (requires shield, most expensive)

  <ansi fg="stat">Special Combat Moves:</ansi>
  - Bash: Variable stamina
  - Trip: Variable stamina
  - Kick: Variable stamina

  <ansi fg="stat">Recovery Actions:</ansi>
  - Stand: 15% of maximum stamina (manual recovery from prone)
  - Auto-recovery: Free (automatic standing attempts)

Note: Defenses cost stamina even when they fail. A single incoming attack can drain
8-11 stamina if all three defenses miss (2+4+5)!

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Low Stamina Penalties ━━━</ansi>

When your stamina drops below 50% of maximum, you suffer severe penalties:

  <ansi fg="red">Combat Penalties:</ansi>
  - <ansi fg="stat">Reduced Hit Chance:</ansi> Harder to land attacks
  - <ansi fg="stat">Reduced Damage:</ansi> Weaker attacks
  - <ansi fg="stat">Reduced Defense:</ansi> Less effective defenses (still cost full stamina!)

  <ansi fg="red">Stamina Exhaustion:</ansi>
  - Cannot use <ansi fg="command">stand</ansi> command if below 15% stamina
  - Some abilities may be restricted at very low stamina

Fighting at low stamina is extremely dangerous. Your defenses still drain stamina
but become less effective, creating a death spiral if you can't regenerate or flee.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Stamina Management Strategy ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="stat">1. Watch Your Stamina:</ansi>
  Monitor stamina in your combat prompt. When it drops below 50%, consider fleeing
  or ending combat to regenerate.

  <ansi fg="stat">2. Choose Defenses Wisely:</ansi>
  Shields are powerful but drain stamina quickly (5 per block). Dodge-focused builds
  are more stamina-efficient (2 per dodge).

  <ansi fg="stat">3. Use Special Moves Tactically:</ansi>
  Don't spam special moves. Use them when knockdown would give a significant advantage,
  not just for extra damage.

  <ansi fg="stat">4. Standing Up:</ansi>
  Auto-recovery is free (costs no stamina), while <ansi fg="command">stand</ansi> costs 15%. Only use
  manual stand when you absolutely must get up immediately.

  <ansi fg="stat">5. Vitality Stat:</ansi>
  Increase your Vitality stat to raise maximum stamina. More stamina = longer fights
  before penalties kick in.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Stamina Regeneration ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="stat">During Combat:</ansi> Slow regeneration (configurable, usually ~2-5 per round)
  <ansi fg="stat">While Resting:</ansi> Fast regeneration when not in combat
  <ansi fg="stat">Vitality Bonus:</ansi> Higher Vitality increases regeneration rate

Stamina regeneration during combat is intentionally slow to make extended fights
challenging. If you're losing the stamina war, flee and recover!

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Improving Maximum Stamina ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="stat">Vitality Stat:</ansi>
  Your primary stamina stat. Every point of Vitality increases max stamina.
  Vitality progresses through use-based mechanics.

  <ansi fg="stat">Equipment:</ansi>
  Some items provide Vitality bonuses, indirectly increasing stamina.

  <ansi fg="stat">Buffs:</ansi>
  Temporary buffs may increase maximum stamina or regeneration rate.

